<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kazan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kazan is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> at its confluence with the Kazanka, the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatarstan">Republic of Tatarstan</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. Founded as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgar</a> fortress, it became the capital of the Khanate of Kazan in the 15th century and was stormed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV</a> in 1552, a victory commemorated by St Basil's Cathedral in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>. It remains the centre of Volga <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatar</a> culture, and its kremlin is a World Heritage Site.</p></div>
